! mcp_bootstrap_p183.strap -- "VERIFY", MCP's tape-label verify
! routine: R VFY at 221161.00 through 221213.40, printed page 183.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.190.  THE HEADER WAS READ, NOT
! ASSUMED, at 400 dpi: "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID LD000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  183".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK. <<<
! Rendered at 400 dpi (crop y=300 H=260 of the full form width): the
! word "LOCATION" is printed at the right-hand end of the heading row
! and NOTHING follows it before the card-serial column -- no digits,
! only the dashed rule.  Nothing was invented off that rule.
!
! That is exactly what docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1 predicts
! for this page: the field is LINE 1'S location, and line 1 here is
! an asterisk banner card that compiles nothing.  The page's first
! LOCATED row is line 4 ("221161.00 * SLC,$"), which is the printed
! p.147 case.  A blank does NOT mean the page has no origin.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-EIGHT PRINTED LINES.  Lines 1-3 are an asterisk banner
! reading "************ VERIFY ************", line 4 is "SLC,$",
! lines 36-37 are two more comment cards in the middle of the code,
! and the other FORTY-TWO lines are instructions.  No DD, no SYN,
! no VF, no XW, NO RESERVATION of any kind, and no forward SLC.
!
! >>> THE PAGE IS CONTIGUOUS AND HAS NO HOLE. <<<  221161.00 to
! 221213.40 -- TWENTY-SEVEN WORDS, forty-two emitted rows of MIXED
! half- and full-word widths, and the counter arrives on the nose at
! every one of the forty-two printed locations.  Nothing is skipped, so neither of
! the two legitimate reasons for a hole (a DR/DRZ reservation, a
! forward SLC) arises here.  The counter LEAVES this page at
! 221214.00.
!
! WHAT THE CODE DOES, off its own printed English:
!
!   lines  5-10  R VFY, the entry.  BB on S SYSTM to R RR if this is
!                a system tape; otherwise clear S TD MOD, S LAB M and
!                S LAB D, clear S VER ("-IF NON SYSTEM, SKIP
!                VERIFY") and branch to Z STEVL.
!   lines 11-18  R RR: set the unit to the installation density
!                (LVI,0,S INST D then SIC/B through K DENST and
!                K K IND / K IO IND), then the channel to the
!                installation mode through K K MODE / K MODE.
!   lines 19-31  issue the read: LVE,9,RV4 plants the return, set
!                S SET UP, save it in R RDL, CNOP to a word boundary,
!                LX/SX stash the I-O instruction, RD reads the label
!                into R RD L, then SIC/B through K SUPP and the
!                K K IND / K IO IND end-op check.
!   lines 32-35  RV4, the return: bring the label word into $R, set
!                S VER, load S C REEL and S EVL MK.
!   lines 38-41  compare the label's reel number against the current
!                one (KF 30 bits at bit 34) and BZAE out to RV3 SCR
!                if they disagree; KVI,0,E MK1A otherwise.
!   lines 42-48  BXE to K W LABL if this is a write; check the label
!                mode (KFI), BAE to K RELOD, record the mode and
!                density into S LAB M / S LABD, and LVI,0,Z STEVL /
!                SV,0,S SCRPM to return.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COUNTED OFF THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN: THIRTY-EIGHT CARDS, AND
! NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The serial column runs LD000001 (line 1) to LD000038 (line 48),
! rendered at 400 dpi and read one serial per line.  THIRTY-EIGHT
! serials for FORTY-EIGHT lines, with no gap in the run: ten serials
! are printed on TWO consecutive lines each, and in every one of the
! ten cases the two lines are a pair of HALF-WORD instructions --
!
!   LD000006 lines  6/ 7   LD000011 lines 12/13   LD000012 lines 14/15
!   LD000014 lines 17/18   LD000019 lines 23/24   LD000021 lines 26/27
!   LD000022 lines 28/29   LD000023 lines 30/31   LD000033 lines 41/42
!   LD000038 lines 47/48
!
! -- which is STRAP's semicolon, the same two-statement card the rest
! of this corpus prints.  38 + 10 = 48 and the arithmetic closes, so
! no line fell off the top or the bottom of the render.
!
!   >>> ALL TEN PAIRS ARE HALF WORD PLUS HALF WORD, AND THE PAIRING
!   WAS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. <<<  printed p.174's deck named this
!   as open -- "WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT: ... a page where a FULL word
!   shares a serial" -- and THIS PAGE IS NOT THAT PAGE.  A first
!   draft of this deck claimed it was, pairing LD000019 with lines
!   24/25 (an SX half word and an RD FULL word); that was an
!   off-by-one in reading the serial column against the line column
!   separately.  Re-rendered as FULL-WIDTH STRIPS so the line number
!   and the serial are in one image, LD000019 is lines 23 AND 24 --
!   "LX,0,$+1.0" and "SX,0,S IO INS($12)", both half words -- and
!   the twelve full words on this page each carry a serial of their
!   own.  So this page CORROBORATES p.174's conjecture and settles
!   nothing against it.  THIS DECK DOES NOT WRITE THE ONE-CARD FORM,
!   because splitting them assembles identically and the per-line
!   listing block is easier to check.)
!
! >>> THE SERIAL PREFIX CHANGES AT THIS PAGE. <<<  Line 1 is
! LD000001, the first card of a new deck.  printed p.176 ends on
! KE000106.  So the serial run does NOT join p.182 to p.183 the way
! it joins p.175 to p.176, and the backward join has to rest on the
! location column -- which it does, see below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN: "SLC,$" AT 221161.00, AND WHAT THAT BUYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 4 prints "221161.00  *  SLC,$" -- an SLC that emits nothing,
! so ITS PRINTED LOCATION IS THE COUNTER ARRIVING FROM printed
! p.182, stated by IBM's own assembler
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE
! item 2).  That is the strongest backward-join witness there is.
!
! >>> AND THIS DECK THROWS IT AWAY, DELIBERATELY AND LOUDLY. <<<
! A deck cannot write "SLC,$" and be assembled alone, so it writes
! the hard "SLC, (8)221161.0".  A hard SLC CANNOT disagree with an
! arriving counter -- it overrides it silently -- so every !CHECK
! below ASSERTS this origin rather than checks it.  The printed
! location is recorded in line 4's listing row so the comparison can
! be made by hand when p.182's deck lands.
!
! PREDICTION FOR p.182, FALSIFIABLE: its last emitted row must leave
! the counter at exactly 221161.00.  If p.182's last printed row is
! a half word it is at 221160.40; if a full word, at 221160.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> EVERY ONE OF THE FORTY-TWO ROWS MATCHED ON THE FIRST
! ASSEMBLY, WITH NO SUBSTITUTION ANYWHERE. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! No printed statement on this page was refused by strap_asm and no
! printed statement had to be rewritten.  Forty-two rows -- TWELVE
! FULL WORDS and THIRTY HALF WORDS, fifty-four printed half words in
! all -- every one bit-identical to the listing.  The
! only departure from the printed characters anywhere in this deck
! is the house convention of closing up the blanks inside a symbol
! name (see below), which is what every landed deck does and what
! the merge requires.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE SYMBOLS ARE PRINTED TWO DIFFERENT WAYS ON THIS ONE PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Read at 900 dpi, the NAME blanks inside an operand are NOT stable:
!
!   line 32 "S SCR PM"   line 48 "S SCRPM"    both word 000006
!   line  8 "S LAB D"    line 46 "S LABD"     both 000007.35
!   line 25 "R RD L"     line 21 "R RDL"      both word 221260
!
! In each pair the two rows compile to the SAME address, so they are
! one symbol printed with different padding, not two symbols.  The
! merged body image resolves all three to a single definition
! (S SCRPM = p.101's "SYN(BU,64),6.0", S LABD = p.101's
! "SYN(BU,1),7.29"), which is independent of this page's ink.
! printed p.152's deck recorded the same phenomenon for this very
! symbol set ("line 6 prints M IOREJ and line 47 prints M IO REJ").
! So the blank is listing padding and the repo's closed-up spelling
! is right; the printed spellings are kept in the listing block.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS, AND WHICH RUNG OF THE LADDER SETTLED EACH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) >>> RUNG 4, THE SAME STATEMENT PRINTED TWICE. <<<  Lines 9 and
!     33 are the same card, "CM0000(BU,1),S VER($11)".  Line 9
!     prints "001000.00 F0"; line 33 prints, to the eye at 900 dpi,
!     "0C1000.CC FC".  Identical cards cannot compile to different
!     words, so line 33's trailing nibble is a DAMAGED 0 and the
!     byte is F0.  Line 33's own octal field settles the direction:
!     "0C1000.CC" holds three round glyphs in fields that can only
!     hold octal digits, so that row is demonstrably dropping ink on
!     round glyphs (rung 5).  The assembler agrees: F0.
!
! (2) >>> THE BRANCH BYTE IS 00, NOT C0, AND THE PAGE PROVES IT FOUR
!     TIMES. <<<  Lines 10, 18 and 29 -- all three of them "B,X" --
!     print their last byte as a round glyph pair that reads "CO" at
!     900 dpi.  Every one is 00, because lines 13, 15, 27 and 31 are
!     the SAME B OPERATION on the SAME PAGE and print a CLOSED "00"
!     in the SAME CHARACTER POSITION.  Open and closed in one
!     character position, one drum, one operation -- rung 4.
!     (Line 22 also prints "CO" and is also 00, but it is CNOP and
!     not a branch, so it rests on a different argument; see (5).)
!
! (3) >>> BZAE's BYTE IS C0 AND THE Z IS VISIBLE. <<<  Line 40
!     prints "221214.76 CC".  Measured through strap_asm, everything
!     else fixed:
!
!         BAE,X   -> C2        BZAE,X  -> C0
!         BXE,X   -> C2        BZXE,X  -> C0
!
!     so this Z CLEARS 0x02 (the BZXL/BXL pattern of printed p.174),
!     it does NOT set 0x04 (the BUSAZ/BUSA pattern of printed
!     p.145).  THE TWO Z's ARE DIFFERENT AND REASONING ACROSS THEM
!     IS A COIN FLIP; the encoder was asked instead.  Line 44 prints
!     BAE's C2 on this same page, so the pair is this page's own
!     control.  The trailing nibble of line 40 is therefore a damaged
!     0, and -- unlike a RESERVATION's Z -- this Z is fully checked.
!
! (4) The LVI byte is 01 and lines 6 and 11 print it "C1".  Lines 16,
!     26 and 47 print a closed "01" for the same operation on this
!     page.  Rung 4.
!
! (5) Line 22 is "CNOP", four characters, read at 900 dpi -- NOT the
!     three-character "NOP" the volume OCR returns for it.  IT IS
!     LOAD-BEARING AND THE TWO ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE: measured,
!     CNOP emits a NOP half word ONLY at an odd half word and
!     nothing at a word boundary, while NOP always emits.  Line 22
!     sits at 221173.40, so both spellings happen to print
!     "000000.30 00" HERE and the !CHECK cannot tell them apart --
!     but CNOP is what puts line 23 at 221174.00, and the ink says
!     CNOP.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE MEASURES ABOUT OTHER PAGES' SYMBOLS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> SIX SIC ROWS, AND ONLY FOUR OF THEM ARE BIT-EXACT READINGS.
! <<<  An UNINDEXED SIC's half word carries the operand's full
! 24-bit bit address, so those are measurements and not
! conventions.  AN INDEXED SIC IS NOT THE SAME THING: it prints the
! DISPLACEMENT, and the bit address never appears.  Counted off the
! listing block, this page has
!
!   lines 14, 30  SIC,K K IND   -> 221371.00 80   BIT-EXACT
!   line  17      SIC,K K MODE  -> 217624.40 80   BIT-EXACT
!   lines 12, 28  SIC,S RET AD($12) -> 000005.00 8C  DISPLACEMENT
!                                                    ONLY -- word 5
!
! K K IND is NEW to the repo and this page pins it to the bit,
! twice.  K K MODE's reading agrees BIT FOR BIT with the value the
! merged body image already carries from printed p.152 -- MEASURED
! against the image (mcp_image.build's symbol table gives bit
! 4711712 = word 0o217624, bit 32), not read out of p.152's deck
! prose.
!
! >>> AND THE SYMBOL ONE WORD BELOW IT IS *NOT* MEASURED. <<<  Lines
! 15 and 31 are "B,K IO IND -> 221370.10 00".  A branch shows only
! bit 32 of its target, so K IO IND is known to the HALF WORD only
! and the ".0" written below is a CONVENTION.  Two adjacent symbols
! on one page, one pinned to the bit and one not -- the difference
! is the operation, not the page.
!
! Z STEVL's bit 32 IS read, and twice by two different operations:
! line 10 "B,Z STEVL -> 221144.50" and line 47 "LVI,0,Z STEVL ->
! 221144.41" both carry the 0o40 half-word select.  The bits BELOW
! 32 are convention.
!
! Likewise R V3 SCR and K RELOD: lines 40 and 44 print ".76", and
! 0o76 = 0o40 | 0o36, where 0o36 is the AE indicator and 0o40 is the
! half-word select (measured: BAE against a target at .00 prints
! ".36", at .40 prints ".76").  So BOTH are at a .40 half word, and
! that is read, not assumed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE OPEN QUESTION THE BRIEF ASKED ABOUT -- AND THIS PAGE DOES
! NOT SETTLE IT. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 32 is "L(BU),S SCR PM($12)", a MODE-ONLY dds against a symbol
! another page defines, and it prints length 000.  printed p.101
! declares "SSCRPM SYN(BU,64), 6.0" -- length SIXTY-FOUR -- and 64
! prints as 000 in a six-bit length field.  BOTH models (inherit, or
! treat "(BU)" as an explicit length 0 whose effLength is 64)
! therefore predict 000 here, so this row is consistent with each
! and discriminates between neither.  THE PAGE SETTLES NOTHING AND
! NOTHING HERE TURNS ON IT.  What would still settle it is unchanged
! from printed p.174's note: a mode-only dds against a symbol whose
! declared length is neither 0 nor 64.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE FORWARD JOIN TO printed p.184, AS A FALSIFIABLE PREDICTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The counter leaves this page at 221214.00 (line 48 is a half word
! at 221213.40).  So:
!
!   printed p.184's first LOCATED row is at 221214.00; and
!   R V3 SCR is DEFINED at 221214.40 on printed p.184.
!
! The second half is a reading of THIS page's ink, not a guess:
! line 40's "BZAE,RV3 SCR -> 221214.76" puts bit 32 of R V3 SCR on,
! and line 44's BAE/K RELOD pair fixes what the 0o40 in a ".76"
! means (measured: BAE against a .00 target prints ".36").
!
! BOTH HALVES ARE MACHINE-CHECKABLE, which is the point of stating
! them this way: a p.184 beginning anywhere but 221214.00 breaks the
! counter, and a p.184 that defines R V3 SCR anywhere but 221214.40
! makes the merged body image REFUSE this deck's SYN.  Neither needs
! a human to notice.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE rows carry it: line 4 (221161.00, the SLC,$), line 23
! (221174.00, "LX,0,$+1.0") and line 43 (221207.40, "KFI(BU,2),0,
! 23").  RECORDED, AND NO RULE IS PROPOSED -- printed p.147 proposed
! one from its own page and printed p.151 refuted it the same
! afternoon.  For the record this page is consistent with p.147's
! "every printed SLC,$ row carries it" (its one SLC does) and is
! another counterexample to any rule that makes the mark exclusive
! to SLCs, since lines 23 and 43 are ordinary instructions in the
! middle of a contiguous run.  Lines 23 and 43 have nothing obvious
! in common with each other either: one is a half word, one a full
! word; one is at .00, one at .40; neither is labelled, branched to,
! first or last.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  The dds on each is the one the DEFINING page prints,
! carried so the merged body image does not refuse the page.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
SSYSTM  SYN(BU,1), 7.25              ! printed p.101 line 23 DEFINES it,
                                     ! "S SYSTM SYN(BU,1),7.25"
                                     ! -SYSTEM TAPE FLAG
STDMOD  SYN(BU,24), 3.0              ! printed p.108 line 9 -STANDARD MODE
SLABM   SYN(BU,2), 7.16              ! printed p.101 line 22 -MODE SPECIFIED IN
SLABD   SYN(BU,1), 7.29              ! printed p.101 line 24 -DENSITY SPECIFIED
                                     ! IN; printed here both as "S LAB D"
                                     ! (line 8) and "S LABD" (line 46)
SVER    SYN(BU,1), 0.40              ! printed p.99 -VERIFY FILE STATUS
SINSTD  SYN(BU,24), 0.0              ! printed p.108 line 6 -INSTALLATION DENSITY
SINSTM  SYN(BU,24), 2.0              ! printed p.108 line 7 -INSTALLATION MODE
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0              ! printed p.101 line 18 -RETURN ADDRESS
SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31              ! printed p.99 -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0              ! printed p.101 line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST
SSCRPM  SYN(BU,64), 6.0              ! printed p.101 line 20 -SCRATCH PAD MEMORY;
                                     ! printed here both as "S SCR PM" (line 32)
                                     ! and "S SCRPM" (line 48)
SCREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.32             ! printed p.101 line 28 -CURRENT REEL ADDRESS
SEVLMK  SYN(BU,19), 2.32             ! printed p.101 line 12 - EVALUATION MASK
SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32              ! printed p.99 line 30 -PRIORITY LEVEL
!
KDENST  SYN, (8)217674.40            ! already in the image from printed p.154;
                                     ! line 13's branch reads bit 32 only
KKMODE  SYN, (8)217624.40            ! already in the image from printed p.152;
                                     ! line 17's SIC reads it TO THE BIT and
                                     ! agrees digit for digit
KMODE   SYN, (8)217615.0             ! already in the image from printed p.152;
                                     ! branch, half word only
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! already in the image from printed p.128;
                                     ! branch, half word only
KWLABL  SYN, (8)217711.0             ! already in the image from printed p.155;
                                     ! line 42's BXE reads bit 32 only
MIOREJ  SYN, (8)221261.0             ! decks p.135 and p.152 already carry this
                                     ! exact value; branch, half word only
!
! NEW TO THE REPO.  Each is back-derived from this page and each one
! is ALSO printed, on a DIFFERENT page, as a defining card -- found
! by grepping the ADDRESS (not the name) in docs/ocr of the volume,
! which is a legitimate INDEX to another page even though it is no
! witness for this one.  Those sightings are recorded, not relied on.
KKIND   SYN, (8)221371.0             ! lines 14/30 SIC it -> BIT-EXACT.
                                     ! OCR index: a label row
                                     ! "221371.00  221371.34 C2  K K IND
                                     ! BRZ,$ -IF NONE ON, ALLS WELL"
KIOIND  SYN, (8)221370.0             ! lines 15/31 BRANCH to it -> half word
                                     ! only, the ".0" is a CONVENTION.
                                     ! OCR index: "221370.00 ... K IO IND
                                     ! L(BU,2),S IO IND($13)"
ZSTEVL  SYN, (8)221144.40            ! lines 10/47 read bit 32 = 1.
                                     ! OCR index: "221144.40  000002.54 3C
                                     ! Z STEVL  LV,0,S EVL MK($12)"
RRDL    SYN, (8)221260.0             ! lines 21/25; branch/offset forms, so
                                     ! bit within the half word unobservable.
                                     ! OCR index: an XW at 221260.00
RV3SCR  SYN, (8)221214.40            ! line 40; the ".40" is READ off the
                                     ! printed ".76", not assumed -- see the
                                     ! forward-join note above
EMK1A   SYN, (8)221152.40            ! line 41; 0o41 = 0o40 | 0o01, so bit 32
                                     ! is read.  OCR index: "221152.40
                                     ! 003000.00+  E MK1A VF,(8)3000."
KRELOD  SYN, (8)221217.40            ! line 44; ".76" again, bit 32 read
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE.  Line numbers are the listing's own.
! Lines 1-3 and 36-37 are comment cards and emit nothing.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)221161.0             ! line 4 prints "SLC,$" at 221161.00 *
RVFY    BB,SSYSTM($12),RRR           ! line  5  R VFY  -TEST IF SYSTEM TAPE
        LVI,0,STDMOD                 ! line  6
        SV,0,SLABM($12)              ! line  7
        CM0000(BU,1),SLABD($12)      ! line  8  -SET LAB DEN TO HIGH FOR UNLAB TAPES
        CM0000(BU,1),SVER($11)       ! line  9  -IF NON SYSTEM, SKIP VERIFY
        B,ZSTEVL                     ! line 10
RRR     LVI,0,SINSTD                 ! line 11  R RR  -SET UNIT TO INSTALLATION DENS
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 12
        B,KDENST                     ! line 13
        SIC,KKIND                    ! line 14
        B,KIOIND                     ! line 15
        LVI,1,SINSTM                 ! line 16  -SET CHAN TO INSTALLATION MODE
        SIC,KKMODE                   ! line 17
        B,KMODE                      ! line 18
        LVE,9,RV4                    ! line 19
        CM1111(BU,1),SSETUP($11)     ! line 20
        SV,9,RRDL                    ! line 21
        CNOP                         ! line 22
        LX,0,$+1.0                   ! line 23                                  *
        SX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line 24
        RD,0.0($14),RRDL             ! line 25  -READ LABEL COMMAND
        LVI,1,$+1.0                  ! line 26
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 27
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 28
        B,KSUPP                      ! line 29
        SIC,KKIND                    ! line 30
        B,KIOIND                     ! line 31  -CHECK IF SUCCESSFUL END OP
RV4     L(BU),SSCRPM($12)            ! line 32  RV4  -BRING LABEL WORD INTO $R
        CM0000(BU,1),SVER($11)       ! line 33
        LV,4,SCREEL($12)             ! line 34
        LV,0,SEVLMK($12)             ! line 35
        BB,SOWNER($11),$+2.32        ! line 38
        KF(BU,30,6),0.34($4),34      ! line 39  -K LAB REEL NO TO CU REEL NO
        BZAE,RV3SCR                  ! line 40  -BRANCH IF THEY DO NOT AGREE
        KVI,0,EMK1A                  ! line 41
        BXE,KWLABL                   ! line 42  -IF $W OR $WEF, REWRITE LABEL
        KFI(BU,2),0,23               ! line 43  -CHECK LABEL MODE               *
        BAE,KRELOD                   ! line 44
        SF(BU,2),SLABM($12),23       ! line 45  -RECORD LABEL MODE
        CM0101(BU,1),SLABD($12),28   ! line 46  -RECORD LABEL DENSITY
        LVI,0,ZSTEVL                 ! line 47
        SV,0,SSCRPM($12)             ! line 48
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, read at 900 dpi for the BINARY OUTPUT column
! and 400 dpi for the LOCATION, LINE and card-serial columns.  The
! second asterisk after the location is the location-column mark.
! Lines 1-3 and 36-37 print no location and no binary.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1                                            * **********...**********   LD000001
!   line  2                                            * ********** VERIFY ******-  LD000002
!   line  3                                            * **********...**********   LD000003
!   line  4  221161.00  *                                SLC,$                     LD000004
!   line  5  221161.00  000007.31 8C 221165.74 02  R VFY BB,S SYSTM($12),R RR       LD000005
!   line  6  221162.00  000003.01 01                     LVI,0,S TD MOD            LD000006
!   line  7  221162.40  000007.01 3C                     SV,0,S LAB M($12)         LD000006
!   line  8  221163.00  000007.35 8C 001000.00 F0        CM0000(BU,1),S LAB D($12) LD000007
!   line  9  221164.00  000000.50 8B 001000.00 F0        CM0000(BU,1),S VER($11)   LD000008
!   line 10  221165.00  221144.50 00                     B,Z STEVL                 LD000009
!   line 11  221165.40  000000.01 01               R RR  LVI,0,S INST D            LD000010
!   line 12  221166.00  000005.00 8C                     SIC,S RET AD($12)         LD000011
!   line 13  221166.40  217674.50 00                     B,K DENST                 LD000011
!   line 14  221167.00  221371.00 80                     SIC,K K IND               LD000012
!   line 15  221167.40  221370.10 00                     B,K IO IND                LD000012
!   line 16  221170.00  000002.03 01                     LVI,1,S INST M            LD000013
!   line 17  221170.40  217624.40 80                     SIC,K K MODE              LD000014
!   line 18  221171.00  217615.10 00                     B,K MODE                  LD000014
!   line 19  221171.40  221201.23 B0                     LVE,9,RV4                 LD000015
