! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DECLARED CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM RVFY   221161.00
!SYM RRR    221165.40
!SYM RV4    221201.00
!
!CHECK 221161.00 | 000007.31 8C 221165.74 02 | line 5 R VFY BB,S SYSTM($12),R RR -TEST IF SYSTEM TAPE -- the page's first emitted row and its entry point; the second half word names THIS page's own line 11, so the branch target is checked against a label the deck defines rather than against a SYN
!CHECK 221162.00 | 000003.01 01 | line 6 LVI,0,S TD MOD -- .01 is 2J+1 for J=0 and the 000003 is S TD MOD's word-3 displacement, not an absolute address; the byte prints "C1" and is 01, settled by lines 16/26/47 printing a closed 01 for LVI on this page
!CHECK 221162.40 | 000007.01 3C | line 7 SV,0,S LAB M($12) -- word 7 is S LAB M's displacement; .01 is 2J+1 for J=0, which is why this row and line 6 differ only in the word
!CHECK 221163.00 | 000007.35 8C 001000.00 F0 | line 8 CM0000(BU,1),S LAB D($12) -SET LAB DEN TO HIGH FOR UNLAB TAPES -- 0o35 = 29 is S LABD's bit within word 7, so this row reads p.101's "SYN(BU,1),7.29" exactly; the connective code is four BINARY digits so "CMOCOO" can only be CM0000
!CHECK 221164.00 | 000000.50 8B 001000.00 F0 | line 9 CM0000(BU,1),S VER($11) -IF NON SYSTEM, SKIP VERIFY -- 0o50 = 40 is S VER's bit in word 0; this row is line 33's control and the pair settles line 33's byte
!CHECK 221165.00 | 221144.50 00 | line 10 B,Z STEVL -- 0o50 = 0o40  OR  0o10, the 0o10 being the branch's own operation bits, so Z STEVL's bit 32 IS read and its lower bits are not; byte prints "CO" and is 00
!CHECK 221165.40 | 000000.01 01 | line 11 R RR LVI,0,S INST D -SET UNIT TO INSTALLATION DENS -- S INST D is word 0 bit 0, so the whole half word is operation bits; line 5's branch lands here
!CHECK 221166.00 | 000005.00 8C | line 12 SIC,S RET AD($12) -- an INDEXED SIC prints the DISPLACEMENT, so this reads S RET AD's word 5 and is NOT the bit-exact absolute reading an unindexed SIC gives; byte 8C's low nibble is the $12
!CHECK 221166.40 | 217674.50 00 | line 13 B,K DENST -- half word only; 0o40 of the 0o50 confirms the ".40" the image already carries for K DENST from printed p.154
!CHECK 221167.00 | 221371.00 80 | line 14 SIC,K K IND -- AN UNINDEXED SIC CARRIES THE FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so this PINS K K IND to 221371.00 to the bit; printed twice on this page (line 30)
!CHECK 221167.40 | 221370.10 00 | line 15 B,K IO IND -- a branch, so only bit 32; K IO IND is one word below the bit-exact K K IND and is known only to the half word. Printed twice (line 31)
!CHECK 221170.00 | 000002.03 01 | line 16 LVI,1,S INST M -SET CHAN TO INSTALLATION MODE -- .03 is 2J+1 for J=1 against line 6's .01 for J=0, which is what makes each the other's control; 000002 is S INST M's word
!CHECK 221170.40 | 217624.40 80 | line 17 SIC,K K MODE -- bit-exact: 221624.40 read off a SIC agrees digit for digit with the K K MODE the merged image already carries from printed p.152
!CHECK 221171.00 | 217615.10 00 | line 18 B,K MODE -- byte prints "CO" and is 00; half word only
!CHECK 221171.40 | 221201.23 B0 | line 19 LVE,9,RV4 -- 0o23 = 19 = 2J+1 for J=9, so the offset field is entirely operation bits and the address is this page's own line 32 at 221201.00. A forward reference inside the page, so it checks the deck's own arithmetic
!CHECK 221172.00 | 000000.37 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 20 CM1111(BU,1),S SET UP($11) -- 0o37 = 31 is S SET UP's bit in word 0; the 0o36 in the second half word is the (BU,1) data description's byte-size field, and it differs from line 8's 0o00 purely because the dds differs. CM1111 against lines 8/9/33's CM0000 on one page is the four-binary-digit code read both ways
!CHECK 221173.00 | 221260.23 30 | line 21 SV,9,R RDL -- 0o23 = 2J+1 for J=9, so R RDL's bit offset is NOT read here; byte 30 is SV
!CHECK 221173.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 22 CNOP -- the same word docs/transcription_workflow.md records for printed p.84 line 7. CNOP emits here because the counter is at an odd half word; see GLYPH CALLS (5) for why "NOP" is not an acceptable reading even though it would print the same
!CHECK 221174.00 | 221175.00 10 | line 23 LX,0,$+1.0 -- "$+1.0" is 221175.00, this page's own next word, so the row checks the deck's counter against the page's; carries a location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221174.40 | 000004.01 1C | line 24 SX,0,S IO INS($12) -- 000004 is S IO INS's word; .01 is 2J+1 for J=0; byte 1C's low nibble is the $12
!CHECK 221175.00 | 000000.00 8E 221260.01 00 | line 25 RD,0.0($14),R RD L -READ LABEL COMMAND -- THE PRINTED MNEMONIC "RD" WAS HANDED TO strap_asm AS PRINTED AND ACCEPTED. Byte 8E's low nibble is the $14; the first operand is the literal 0.0 and the second half word is R RDL's half word. This is the row whose card serial LD000019 it shares with line 24, a HALF word and a FULL word on one card
!CHECK 221176.00 | 221177.03 01 | line 26 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- "$+1.0" is 221177.00; .03 is 2J+1 for J=1, so this row and line 23 together read the page's own counter at two places
!CHECK 221176.40 | 221261.10 00 | line 27 B,M IO REJ -- M IOREJ at 221261.00 is already carried by decks p.135 and p.152 at this exact value; half word only
!CHECK 221177.00 | 000005.00 8C | line 28 SIC,S RET AD($12) -- bit-identical to line 12, the same statement printed twice on one page
!CHECK 221177.40 | 216242.10 00 | line 29 B,K SUPP -- byte prints "CO" and is 00; K SUPP's half word confirms printed p.128's value
!CHECK 221200.00 | 221371.00 80 | line 30 SIC,K K IND -- bit-identical to line 14, which is what makes the bit-exact reading of K K IND a reading twice over
!CHECK 221200.40 | 221370.10 00 | line 31 B,K IO IND -CHECK IF SUCCESSFUL END OP -- bit-identical to line 15
!CHECK 221201.00 | 000006.00 8C 000000.20 50 | line 32 RV4 L(BU),S SCR PM($12) -BRING LABEL WORD INTO $R -- line 19's LVE target. THE PRINTED LENGTH 000 PINS NOTHING: p.101 declares S SCRPM (BU,64) and 64 prints as 000 in a six-bit field, so a mode-only "(BU)" and an inherited 64 are indistinguishable here
!CHECK 221202.00 | 000000.50 8B 001000.00 F0 | line 33 CM0000(BU,1),S VER($11) -- BIT-IDENTICAL TO LINE 9 AND THAT IS WHAT SETTLES IT: the page prints this row's octal field as "0C1000.CC" and its byte as "FC", four open round glyphs, and identical cards cannot compile to different words
!CHECK 221203.00 | 000010.50 3C | line 34 LV,4,S C REEL($12) -- 0o50 = 0o40  OR  0o10, where 0o40 is S C REEL's bit 32 within word 8 (p.101's "SYN(BU,18),8.32") and 0o10 is 2J for J=4; byte 3C is LV
!CHECK 221203.40 | 000002.40 3C | line 35 LV,0,S EVL MK($12) -- 0o40 is S EVL MK's bit 32 within word 2 and 2J = 0 for J=0, so this row and line 34 together separate the two contributions to line 34's 0o50
!CHECK 221204.00 | 000000.40 8B 221206.74 02 | line 38 BB,SOWNER($11),$+2.32 -- 0o40 = 32 is SOWNER's bit in word 0; "$+2.32" is 221206.40 and prints 0o74 = 0o40  OR  0o34, the 0o34 being BB's operation bits, which line 5 prints identically against a label
!CHECK 221205.00 | 000000.42 84 036621.23 10 | line 39 KF(BU,30,6),0.34($4),34 -K LAB REEL NO TO CU REEL NO -- 0o42 = 34 DECIMAL, so the ".34" is read decimal and an octal reading would fail this row; 0o036 is the length 30 and the 6 is the byte size; byte 84's low nibble is the $4
!CHECK 221206.00 | 221214.76 C0 | line 40 BZAE,RV3 SCR -BRANCH IF THEY DO NOT AGREE -- 0o76 = 0o40  OR  0o36, so R V3 SCR's bit 32 IS read and it is at 221214.40. Byte C0 against line 44's BAE C2: THIS Z CLEARS 0x02, it does not set 0x04, and it is fully visible
!CHECK 221206.40 | 221152.41 04 | line 41 KVI,0,E MK1A -- 0o41 = 0o40  OR  0o01, so E MK1A's bit 32 is read; the volume OCR indexes a VF defining card at 221152.40 on another page
!CHECK 221207.00 | 217711.32 C2 | line 42 BXE,K W LABL -IF $W OR $WEF, REWRITE LABEL -- 0o32 is the XE indicator with NO 0o40, so K W LABL is at a .00 half word, which agrees with the value the merged image already carries from printed p.155
!CHECK 221207.40 | 000000.00 80 402013.63 10 | line 43 KFI(BU,2),0,23 -CHECK LABEL MODE -- A FULL WORD AT AN ODD HALF WORD. It straddles 221207.40 and 221210.00, which is the only way line 44 lands at 221210.40, and strap_asm places it correctly; the immediate 0 is left-justified in the A24 field, which is what the 402013 records. Carries a location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221210.40 | 221217.76 C2 | line 44 BAE,K RELOD -- 0o76 again: K RELOD is at 221217.40. Measured against line 40, BAE's C2 and BZAE's C0 differ by the Z alone
!CHECK 221211.00 | 000007.20 8C 002013.52 F0 | line 45 SF(BU,2),S LAB M($12),23 -RECORD LABEL MODE -- 0o20 = 16 is S LAB M's bit within word 7, so this row reads p.101's "SYN(BU,2),7.16" exactly; 0o002 is the explicit length 2 and 0o23 the offset 23 is not independently visible
!CHECK 221212.00 | 000007.35 8C 001016.12 F0 | line 46 CM0101(BU,1),S LABD($12),28 -RECORD LABEL DENSITY -- the same 0o35 = 29 as line 8 against the SAME symbol spelled "S LABD" here and "S LAB D" there, which is the strongest evidence the blank is listing padding; CM0101 against CM0000 and CM1111 on one page is three readings of the four-binary-digit code
!CHECK 221213.00 | 221144.41 01 | line 47 LVI,0,Z STEVL -- 0o41 = 0o40  OR  0o01, so Z STEVL's bit 32 is read HERE BY A SECOND OPERATION, line 10 having read it with a branch. Two operations, one symbol, same answer
!CHECK 221213.40 | 000006.01 3C | line 48 SV,0,S SCRPM($12) -- the page's last emitted row; word 6 is S SCRPM's displacement and .01 is 2J+1 for J=0. The counter leaves this page at 221214.00
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS DECK COULD NOT SETTLE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (A) THE BACKWARD JOIN IS NOT CHECKED BY ANYTHING HERE.  The page
!     PRINTS "SLC,$" and the deck writes a hard SLC, so the origin
!     is asserted.  The printed 221161.00 is in the listing block
!     and nothing but a hand comparison with printed p.182 closes
!     it.  The card-serial column cannot help either, because this
!     page starts a NEW deck at LD000001.
!
! (B) THE BIT OFFSETS OF K IO IND, K MODE, K SUPP, K W LABL,
!     M IOREJ AND R RDL ARE UNOBSERVABLE BELOW BIT 32 from this
!     page.  Writing ".0" is a CONVENTION.  The half word itself IS
!     checked and would fail if wrong.  K DENST, K K MODE, Z STEVL,
!     R V3 SCR, E MK1A and K RELOD have their bit 32 READ (they all
!     print a 0o40), and K K IND alone is pinned to the BIT by its
!     SIC.
!
! (C) WHETHER R RDL IS REALLY ONE SYMBOL.  Line 21 prints "R RDL"
!     and line 25 prints "R RD L", both resolving to word 221260,
!     and the volume OCR indexes an XW defining card at 221260.00 on
!     a later page -- but that defining card has NOT been rendered
!     and this deck's SYN is back-derived from this page's own two
!     rows.  WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT: rendering the page that prints
!     221260.00 in its LOCATION column.
!
! (D) THE SIX COMMENT CARDS ARE QUOTED, NOT TRANSCRIBED CHARACTER BY
!     CHARACTER.  Lines 1, 3 and the asterisk runs on 2, 36 and 37
!     are rows of asterisks and counting them off a worn drum is a
!     reading nobody can check.  The PROSE in them -- "VERIFY",
!     "NOP FOLLOWING COMMAND IF CHECKING", "OF MCP REEL LABELS
!     DESIRED" -- was read at 400 dpi across the full form width and
!     is quoted in full.
!
! (E) WHAT LINES 36-37 ARE TELLING AN OPERATOR TO DO.  They say to
!     NOP the FOLLOWING command -- line 38's BB -- if MCP reel-label
!     checking is wanted.  That is the listing's own English and it
!     is recorded, but nothing here establishes who does the NOPing
!     or when, and rule 1 forbids inferring it from how the code
!     looks.
!
! (F) THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK ON LINES 23 AND 43.  See above:
!     recorded, no rule proposed, and this page alone cannot produce
!     one.
